              <span>●</span> type=gha (Actions Cache)
            </h3>
            <ul class="text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li><strong>Zero Credential Friction:</strong> Authenticates seamlessly using native GitHub Action workflow tokens without external secrets.</li>
              <li><strong>Hyper-Localized Transport:</strong> Layer blobs are served directly from Azure/AWS internal caching storage collocated with GitHub-hosted runners.</li>
              <li><strong>Scope Isolation:</strong> Branch scoping rules apply: PR workflows can access caches from the base/default branch (<code class="text-slate-200">main</code>), preventing cache pollution across feature branches.</li>
              <li><strong>10 GB Quota Limit:</strong> Repository cache is capped at 10 GB; aggressively evicted via Least-Recently-Used (LRU).</li>
            </ul>
